    "title": "Interlanguage and Mathematical Translation Methodology Sidecar (Post-2DE Route-Context Delta)",
    "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.21247868",
    "publication_date": "2026-07-07",
    "description": "<p>This record preserves the interlanguage and constructed-language methodology sidecar for the Modern LaTeX Manuscripts project: Interslavic and Slavic translation governance, weighted automaton and term-weight ledgers, CJK/Arabic/RTL/Persianate source-body support packages, and Claude/ChatGPT/Fable provenance materials.</p><p><strong>Read first:</strong> <code>00_Interlanguage_Methodology_Current_20260706.pdf</code>. This version keeps the July 6 front files and the grouped side-branch payloads from the previous version, and adds a small post-2DE route-context delta from <code>origin/codex/noether-pc-20260629</code> at commit <code>516abae30</code>. The new file <code>10_Interlanguage_OtherPC_Post2DE_RouteContext_Returns_20260707.zip</code> contains 257 exported branch files plus manifest/summary wrappers: route-context returns, Persianate/Tajik source-use gap ledgers, non-Slavic route packets, and transfer-audit rows.</p><p><strong>Status caveat.</strong> This is methodology, source-body routing, provenance, and corpus-infrastructure material. It is not a certified language edition, not native-speaker approval, not accepted terminology, not source-fidelity certification, not a reader output, and not proof that any language branch is complete. Generated draft material may propose terms and expose inconsistencies, but source-body and independent/native witness status remain separate from generated translation status.</p><p><strong>GitHub.</strong> Corrections, added source bodies, better weighting heuristics, and cleaned language-branch packages can be suggested via issues or pull requests at <a href=\"https://github.com/KokunoYumeto/modern-latex-manuscripts\">https://github.com/KokunoYumeto/modern-latex-manuscripts</a>.</p>",
